ovider-wide restart protocol is strong: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state, restart scheduling and observed loss of reachability, a changed boot identity independently confirmed by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service, identities, permissions, document, and protocol behavior. The only material quality issue is retained temporary test residue.","limitations":["The lifecycle failed-service probe was unsupported because it checks systemd on Alpine; direct OpenRC status checks nevertheless showed statusd started before and after reboot.","The lifecycle network-socket inventory does not enumerate Unix-domain sockets, so the required socket state relies on direct executor stat and behavior evidence.","Temporary test artifacts were not cleaned from /tmp after evidence collection."]}
